WEBVTT

1
00:00:28.291 --> 00:00:31.833
In verse 14.16,

2
00:00:31.833 --> 00:00:33.083
Lord Krishna explains that

3
00:00:33.083 --> 00:00:36.291
when a person acts under the influence
of the three gunas –

4
00:00:36.291 --> 00:00:38.708
sattva, rajas, and tamas –

5
00:00:38.708 --> 00:00:41.958
the results of those actions differ too.

6
00:00:41.958 --> 00:00:45.875
The nature of sattva is knowledge and peace,

7
00:00:45.875 --> 00:00:47.333
the nature of rajas is

8
00:00:47.333 --> 00:00:50.208
desire and the tendency toward action,

9
00:00:50.208 --> 00:00:52.166
and the nature of tamas is

10
00:00:52.166 --> 00:00:55.875
ignorance, laziness, and inertia.

11
00:00:55.875 --> 00:00:58.708
These results affect not only this life,

12
00:00:58.708 --> 00:01:02.708
but also the soul’s journey ahead.

13
00:01:07.375 --> 00:01:09.625
Action performed in sattva Guna,

14
00:01:09.625 --> 00:01:13.833
when done with a selfless spirit and discipline,

15
00:01:13.833 --> 00:01:19.791
yields purity and inner contentment.

16
00:01:19.791 --> 00:01:22.375
It elevates the soul

17
00:01:22.375 --> 00:01:25.125
and leads it toward knowledge.

18
00:01:25.125 --> 00:01:28.000
Action performed in Rajo Guna is
driven by desire

19
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:31.083
and attachment to outcomes.

20
00:01:31.083 --> 00:01:32.000
Such actions

21
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:34.791
do bring brief pleasure,

22
00:01:34.791 --> 00:01:38.125
but ultimately leave exhaustion, dissatisfaction,

23
00:01:38.125 --> 00:01:42.458
and bind the soul again in the cycle
of birth and death.

24
00:01:42.458 --> 00:01:45.541
Actions influenced by Tamo Guna are
filled with laziness,

25
00:01:45.541 --> 00:01:49.000
carelessness, and ignorance.

26
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:52.708
Their result is deeper ignorance –

27
00:01:52.708 --> 00:01:53.583
which makes the soul

28
00:01:53.583 --> 00:01:56.958
forget its true identity

29
00:01:56.958 --> 00:02:00.916
and traps it further in darkness.

30
00:02:00.916 --> 00:02:04.916
Lord Krishna explains that a person
who gradually

31
00:02:04.916 --> 00:02:08.958
rises above rajas and tamas and
moves toward sattva

32
00:02:08.958 --> 00:02:11.333
purifies their heart

33
00:02:11.333 --> 00:02:14.583
and moves toward liberation.

34
00:02:14.583 --> 00:02:15.958
But the goal

35
00:02:15.958 --> 00:02:18.625
is not only to remain in sattva.

36
00:02:18.625 --> 00:02:21.291
Through devotion and spiritual knowledge,

37
00:02:21.291 --> 00:02:24.666
a person can cross the bondage of
all three gunas

38
00:02:24.666 --> 00:02:28.000
and move toward the supreme goal – liberation.

39
00:02:32.916 --> 00:02:34.500
Sometimes

40
00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:38.000
you limit your day

41
00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:44.666
to simply completing a to-do list.

42
00:02:44.666 --> 00:02:47.250
At the end of the day you think –

43
00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:49.708
‘what did I do today?’ –

44
00:02:49.708 --> 00:02:54.541
as if this alone were the measure of progress.

45
00:02:54.541 --> 00:02:57.416
But the Gita

46
00:02:57.416 --> 00:03:01.458
gives us a deeper lens.

47
00:03:01.458 --> 00:03:04.291
The question is not only

48
00:03:04.291 --> 00:03:07.375
what I did, but

49
00:03:07.375 --> 00:03:11.000
in what spirit I did it.

50
00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:14.375
Two people can do the same work –

51
00:03:14.375 --> 00:03:16.416
like cooking a meal

52
00:03:16.416 --> 00:03:19.166
or leading a meeting.

53
00:03:19.166 --> 00:03:23.166
But the guna in which that work was done

54
00:03:23.166 --> 00:03:27.041
completely changes its outcome.

55
00:03:27.041 --> 00:03:30.083
Action in sattva –

56
00:03:30.083 --> 00:03:34.000
with clarity, honesty, and alertness –

57
00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:37.916
yields peace and growth. Action in rajas –

58
00:03:37.916 --> 00:03:40.666
driven by ego, haste,

59
00:03:40.666 --> 00:03:44.000
or restlessness – may appear
successful outwardly,

60
00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:48.250
but leaves tiredness and dissatisfaction within.

61
00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:51.333
Action in tamas – from carelessness

62
00:03:51.333 --> 00:03:56.833
or mere formality – pulls you downward,

63
00:03:56.833 --> 00:04:00.083
even if the task gets done.

64
00:04:00.083 --> 00:04:02.958
So now ask yourself –

65
00:04:02.958 --> 00:04:05.791
‘Was I alert?

66
00:04:05.791 --> 00:04:08.583
Was I kind?

67
00:04:08.583 --> 00:04:10.833
Was I calm?’

68
00:04:10.833 --> 00:04:13.375
Because these are the signs

69
00:04:13.375 --> 00:04:16.708
of which guna you were acting in.

70
00:04:16.708 --> 00:04:19.416
It is not about doing more –

71
00:04:19.416 --> 00:04:21.875
it is about doing with awareness.

72
00:04:21.875 --> 00:04:26.500
This is where real transformation begins.

73
00:04:31.208 --> 00:04:32.500
Every family

74
00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:37.416
wants peace and a sense of belonging.
But without

75
00:04:37.416 --> 00:04:41.250
realising it, we sometimes sow seeds

76
00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:44.916
that create tension and distance.

77
00:04:44.916 --> 00:04:48.375
Harsh words, avoiding necessary conversations,

78
00:04:48.375 --> 00:04:51.375
or overlooking small needs –

79
00:04:51.375 --> 00:04:55.583
these are the seeds of rajas and tamas.

80
00:04:55.583 --> 00:04:57.916
And then we wonder –

81
00:04:57.916 --> 00:05:01.875
why has the atmosphere at home
become heavy?

82
00:05:01.875 --> 00:05:04.250
The truth is simple –

83
00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:08.875
as you sow, so you reap.

84
00:05:08.875 --> 00:05:11.916
If you want harmony at home,

85
00:05:11.916 --> 00:05:15.041
you must sow the seeds of sattva Guna.

86
00:05:15.041 --> 00:05:19.000
Gentle words, quality time,

87
00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:23.000
meals prepared with love, a clean atmosphere –

88
00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:26.541
these small steps make a big difference.

89
00:05:26.541 --> 00:05:28.208
Imagine –

90
00:05:28.208 --> 00:05:32.083
one home where everyone rises on time,

91
00:05:32.083 --> 00:05:35.333
gets ready and begins their day purposefully,

92
00:05:35.333 --> 00:05:40.083
where the atmosphere is sacred
through prayer and the Gita.

93
00:05:40.083 --> 00:05:42.375
And another home –

94
00:05:42.375 --> 00:05:45.958
where late nights of tamasic habits

95
00:05:45.958 --> 00:05:48.666
lead to a morning of rush

96
00:05:48.666 --> 00:05:50.416
and irritability.

97
00:05:50.416 --> 00:05:54.583
Which home’s day will be joyful – you can

98
00:05:54.583 --> 00:05:56.958
see for yourself.

99
00:05:56.958 --> 00:05:58.541
The Gita says –

100
00:05:58.541 --> 00:06:00.916
actions done in tamas

101
00:06:00.916 --> 00:06:03.875
bring only more confusion.

102
00:06:03.875 --> 00:06:08.208
So when you raise your voice out of tiredness

103
00:06:08.208 --> 00:06:11.375
or brush aside a child’s words out of laziness,

104
00:06:11.375 --> 00:06:14.291
you are sowing the wrong seeds.

105
00:06:14.291 --> 00:06:19.833
Pause and ask yourself – ‘Is this the energy

106
00:06:19.833 --> 00:06:23.916
I want to grow in my home?’

107
00:06:23.916 --> 00:06:27.375
If not – change.

108
00:06:27.375 --> 00:06:28.875
A sattvic family

109
00:06:28.875 --> 00:06:33.000
life is sown and tended every day –

110
00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:35.500
with every aware and conscious choice.

111
00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:42.458
At your workplace,

112
00:06:42.458 --> 00:06:44.416
do not only look at

113
00:06:44.416 --> 00:06:46.791
how much work you are doing.

114
00:06:46.791 --> 00:06:51.958
Also look at how you are doing it.

115
00:06:51.958 --> 00:06:56.083
Whether you are a manager or an employee –

116
00:06:56.083 --> 00:06:59.541
do not work only for salary or promotion.

117
00:06:59.541 --> 00:07:01.166
See it as an opportunity

118
00:07:01.166 --> 00:07:03.666
to contribute your best.

119
00:07:03.666 --> 00:07:05.708
Because this is sattva Guna –

120
00:07:05.708 --> 00:07:08.708
which is beneficial not only for you,
but for the entire

121
00:07:08.708 --> 00:07:12.000
organisation and society.

122
00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:15.000
Look, Rajas-driven effort

123
00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:17.250
appears productive on the surface.

124
00:07:17.250 --> 00:07:21.291
Long nights, constant rushing, high targets.

125
00:07:21.291 --> 00:07:26.208
But within, it leaves restlessness
and dissatisfaction.

126
00:07:26.208 --> 00:07:27.833
One goal arrives

127
00:07:27.833 --> 00:07:31.625
and immediately another stands before you.

128
00:07:31.625 --> 00:07:36.041
Contentment moves further away
instead of closer.

129
00:07:36.041 --> 00:07:39.208
This is the nature of Rajo Guna. And when

130
00:07:39.208 --> 00:07:42.291
work is influenced by tamas –

131
00:07:42.291 --> 00:07:45.375
carelessly, without clear direction –

132
00:07:45.375 --> 00:07:48.416
you may complete the list,

133
00:07:48.416 --> 00:07:52.375
but the result is stagnation.

134
00:07:52.375 --> 00:07:55.458
Procrastination, shortcuts, or indifference –

135
00:07:55.458 --> 00:07:58.583
these are all signs of effort

136
00:07:58.583 --> 00:08:01.000
that has become fruitless.

137
00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:04.333
But when you act from sattva Guna,

138
00:08:04.333 --> 00:08:05.625
your effort becomes

139
00:08:05.625 --> 00:08:09.541
calm, clear, and meaningful.

140
00:08:09.541 --> 00:08:12.250
You are less reactive

141
00:08:12.250 --> 00:08:14.250
and more alert.

142
00:08:14.250 --> 00:08:16.875
Your identity comes not from busyness,

143
00:08:16.875 --> 00:08:19.208
but from integrity.

144
00:08:19.208 --> 00:08:22.416
The result? Progress alongside peace –

145
00:08:22.416 --> 00:08:25.375
a fulfilment that does not exhaust.

146
00:08:25.375 --> 00:08:29.500
So pause at work and ask yourself –

147
00:08:29.500 --> 00:08:34.000
‘Which guna is driving my effort?

148
00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:37.583
Am I truly building something lasting,

149
00:08:37.583 --> 00:08:38.750
or only feeding a cycle

150
00:08:38.750 --> 00:08:41.750
of stress and stagnation?’

151
00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:45.833
Ground your actions in sattva Guna.

152
00:08:45.833 --> 00:08:49.166
This effort brings true progress –

153
00:08:49.166 --> 00:08:52.208
not only in work, but within.
